{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said: The outcry of Sodom and Gomorrah, because it is great, I will go down now, etc.</b> The verses are joined one to the other: it means — the outcry of Sodom and Gomorrah and their sin, which is very great, I will go down and see; if all of them sinned, and if not, I will know who the sinners are. This sin was that they possessed within them all the evil traits, as our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״ואנשי סדום רעים וחטאים״ — 'and the men of Sodom were wicked and sinners' — wicked in their money, as is said (Deuteronomy 15:9) ״ורעה עינך באחיך האביון״; and sinners in their bodies, as is written (Genesis 39:9) ״וחטאתי לאלהים״. 'To YHWH' — this is the blessing of the Name. 'Very' — this is bloodshed, as is said (II Kings 21:16) ״וגם דם נקי שפך מנשה הרבה מאד״. But their sentence was sealed for the sin that they despised charity and paid no heed to their poor and their needy who lay starving. And this is what the verse explained by way of the plain sense (peshat): ״ואנשי סדום רעים וחטאים לה' מאד״ — that their sin reached to HaShem, in the manner of what is written concerning the poor (Deuteronomy 15:9): ״וקרא עליך אל ה' והיה בך חטא״. And the prophet testified likewise, saying (Ezekiel 16:49): הנה זה היה עון סדום אחותך גאון שבעת לחם ושלות השקט היה לה ולבנותיה ויד עני ואביון לא החזיקה, and it is written (ibid.): ותגבהנה ותעשנה תועבה לפני ואסיר אתהן כאשר ראיתי. And because they were constant in this sin, therefore their sentence was sealed upon it — for there is no nation in the world that does not practice charity one with another, but the men of Sodom despised it and were cruel to the utmost. And even though the Torah had not yet been given, charity is among the commandments grasped by reason, and it is an abominable thing that a person should see one of his own kind lying in starvation while he is rich and sated with all good and does not have pity on him to sustain his life — how much the more so upon one who is of his faith and dwells with him in one city. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, brought destruction upon the men of Sodom because they withheld it, and exacted the vengeance of the poor. And from this our Rabbis of blessed memory derived: the vengeance of the gentile nations is in the hand of Israel, and the vengeance of Israel is in the hand of their poor. The vengeance of the gentile nations is in the hand of Israel, as is said (Ezekiel 25:14): ״ונתתי את נקמתי באדום ביד עמי ישראל״. And the vengeance of Israel is in the hand of their poor, as is said (Deuteronomy 15:9): ״וקרא עליך אל ה' והיה בך חטא״. Its meaning is that wealth is not given to the rich except to test by it how he will conduct himself. Rabbi said: once this poor man stands at your door, the Holy One, blessed be He, stands at his right hand; if you gave to him, this One who stands at his right hand blesses you, and if not, this One who stands at his right hand exacts retribution from you, as is said (Psalms 109:31): ״כי יעמוד לימין אביון״. One verse says (Proverbs 22:2): ״עשיר ורש נפגשו עושה כלם ה'״, and another verse says (ibid. 22:29 — per the citation as written): ״רש ואיש תככים נפגשו מאיר עיני שניהם ה'״. How so? Here, when he gave to him; here, when he did not give to him." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״זעקת סדום ועמורה כי רבה״ — 'The outcry of Sodom and Gomorrah, because it is great.' That was the rich woman who would bring out bread for the poor in a basket; the matter became known: they smeared it with honey and set it on a beam of the bridge; flies came and ate it. This is what is written: ״זעקת סדום ועמורה כי רבה״ — on account of the matter of the rich woman (ריבה)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The citation in comment 0 reads '(שם כט)' i.e. Proverbs 22:29, but the verse 'רש ואיש תככים נפגשו מאיר עיני שניהם ה'' is Proverbs 29:13 (though it opens with 'רש ואיש תככים'); the citation as written points to 22:29. The Aramaic midrashic narrative in comment 1 is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:40.199017262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}